WEBVTT

00:01.000 --> 00:02.240
[opening theme playing]

01:24.280 --> 01:25.520
[tapping on door]

01:25.600 --> 01:28.000
Open up, love.

01:28.080 --> 01:29.720
I brought more things
for you and the baby.

01:29.800 --> 01:33.320
Got some fresh eggs and bread.
I'll leave it here.

01:33.400 --> 01:35.400
[baby crying]

01:35.480 --> 01:37.680
-Ada, think of the little one.
-Shh.

01:39.360 --> 01:41.320
Babies don't have principles.

01:41.400 --> 01:42.600
[baby cooing]

01:48.440 --> 01:49.880
[baby crying]

02:10.280 --> 02:11.720
Did you speak to her?

02:12.880 --> 02:14.320
She didn't speak back.

02:17.680 --> 02:19.120
Well, did you tell her?

02:20.720 --> 02:23.240
I'll only tell her what I know to be true.

02:25.720 --> 02:28.160
It's the last time I am going to say this.

02:28.240 --> 02:31.280
It wasn't me who shopped Freddie Thorne.

02:33.560 --> 02:34.960
Tommy.

02:35.040 --> 02:37.040
I'd ask you to swear on the Bible,

02:37.120 --> 02:40.280
but you can't swear on that, can you?

02:40.360 --> 02:41.680
Nothing you hold sacred.

02:52.160 --> 02:53.320
There's tea.

02:59.200 --> 03:00.560
The new system.

03:01.680 --> 03:03.520
Everything in the diary, eh?

03:03.600 --> 03:04.680
Mm-hmm.

03:09.880 --> 03:12.280
Black star. What does that mean?

03:12.840 --> 03:15.080
The black star day

03:15.160 --> 03:18.280
is the day we take out
Billy Kimber and his men.

03:18.840 --> 03:20.240
No one knows this.

03:21.360 --> 03:22.720
Not even your family?

03:24.440 --> 03:25.800
Grace.

03:28.480 --> 03:31.400
Everyone in my family hates me.

03:31.480 --> 03:32.640
Why would I tell them?

03:35.880 --> 03:38.240
He's off the bloody rails is what he is.

03:38.320 --> 03:40.400
If he'll turn nose on his best mate...

03:40.480 --> 03:43.560
Bloody neighbors, John.
Snitch behind the curtain.

03:43.640 --> 03:47.360
Yeah, well, if you think that,
you're the only one who does.

03:47.440 --> 03:49.120
Look at this, look.

03:49.200 --> 03:52.240
Bloody raking it in.
Who's running this carny?

03:52.320 --> 03:53.880
Name of Marston.

03:53.960 --> 03:55.800
Intends on wintering
in Small Heath with this ring.

03:55.880 --> 03:58.040
-Does he?
-Only heard.

03:58.120 --> 04:02.880
Nobody in Small Heath craps in a pot
without the decree of Tommy Almighty.

04:02.960 --> 04:06.560
Mr. Marston, I believe. The ringmaster!

04:06.640 --> 04:08.000
-Proud I am to say so.
-Yes, well,

04:08.080 --> 04:10.800
these here are civilized parts.

04:10.880 --> 04:14.120
Man wants to set his stall up
with fellas lamping each other,

04:14.200 --> 04:16.040
he needs himself a license.

04:16.120 --> 04:17.200
A license?

04:18.440 --> 04:21.519
For a fee. From those in charge.

04:22.560 --> 04:23.680
[men cheering]

04:23.760 --> 04:26.400
I'll tell you what.
How about I keep my money,

04:26.480 --> 04:28.560
and you shove a license
up your arse crack?

04:28.640 --> 04:30.280
You don't want to speak to me like that.

04:30.360 --> 04:32.040
And who the bloody hell
do you think you are?

04:32.120 --> 04:35.040
My name is Arthur Shelby!

04:37.080 --> 04:38.400
Dad?

04:44.600 --> 04:45.680
Jesus!

04:51.280 --> 04:52.960
Thank you. You are a good boy.

04:56.080 --> 04:58.640
Bless thee, Father, for these bounties
we are about to receive--

04:58.720 --> 05:00.320
Jesus Christ.

05:00.400 --> 05:03.200
Please, woman, not in vain.

05:04.560 --> 05:06.400
Finish your sandwich and sling your hook.

05:08.120 --> 05:12.000
Pollyanna. I'm the guest
of the head of this family,

05:12.080 --> 05:15.000
so why don't you maybe tend
to your mangle or your scuttle?

05:15.080 --> 05:16.880
The head of the family ain't here.

05:21.480 --> 05:22.680
Tommy.

05:22.760 --> 05:26.080
He sometimes helps me
with... with business, Dad.

05:26.160 --> 05:29.320
[door opens, closes]

05:29.400 --> 05:31.440
Aye, well, speak of the devil.

05:33.400 --> 05:34.680
How are you, son?

05:36.600 --> 05:37.880
Get out.

05:38.720 --> 05:39.680
Come on, son.

05:40.760 --> 05:42.040
I'm a changed man.

05:43.200 --> 05:46.400
This family needed you ten years ago,

05:46.480 --> 05:48.520
and you walked out on us.

05:48.600 --> 05:50.920
Not now. Get out of this house.

05:51.280 --> 05:53.440
-Tommy, he's different--
-Shut up.

05:56.640 --> 05:58.000
It's all right, son.

05:59.760 --> 06:03.400
Arthur Shelby never stays
where he's not welcome.

06:09.640 --> 06:11.520
Quite something you've become.

06:17.360 --> 06:18.520
Bye, son.

06:29.960 --> 06:30.960
He's our dad.

06:31.040 --> 06:32.240
[sighs]

06:33.600 --> 06:35.080
He's a selfish bastard.

06:37.520 --> 06:39.600
You calling someone a selfish bastard,

06:41.520 --> 06:43.440
that's a bit rich, Tommy.

06:43.520 --> 06:46.120
I mean, thanks to you,

06:46.200 --> 06:48.000
we're already down a bloody sister.

06:49.400 --> 06:52.200
You want to see him, Arthur?
You want to see him?

06:53.520 --> 06:54.840
You go with him.

07:11.000 --> 07:12.840
[door opens, slams]

07:24.200 --> 07:28.960
Grace, I am taking five pounds
from petty cash, all right?

07:29.040 --> 07:30.840
[Grace] We don't have
five pounds in petty cash.

07:30.920 --> 07:32.640
Then I'll take what we've got.

07:32.720 --> 07:34.040
Count it and leave a receipt.

07:36.480 --> 07:39.880
Arthur, there are things
in these books I don't understand.

07:39.960 --> 07:43.000
-Likewise.
-Every week we pay one pound ten shilling

07:43.080 --> 07:47.600
by postal order
to a Daniel Owen in London.

07:47.680 --> 07:52.360
Danny Whizz-Bang, hangs around
the pubs in Camden Town Wharf for us.

07:52.440 --> 07:55.080
Keeps his ears open for business.
He's a good man.

07:55.160 --> 07:56.560
I thought Danny Whizz-Bang was dead.

07:56.640 --> 07:58.640
Then you thought wrong, didn't you?

07:58.720 --> 08:00.720
But I've seen his grave. He was shot.

08:01.560 --> 08:04.320
That was a show to satisfy the wops.

08:04.400 --> 08:06.680
Tommy just shot
some sheep's brains at him.

08:08.080 --> 08:09.600
Who's buried in his grave?

08:14.360 --> 08:18.480
Now, look, Grace,
if you know what's good for you,

08:18.560 --> 08:22.160
you don't ask questions
about things that don't concern you.

08:22.240 --> 08:23.680
Never. Right?

08:25.200 --> 08:28.080
That's for you.
And don't tell Tommy I took this!

08:58.400 --> 09:00.400
The boy needs a good hiding,
if you ask me.

09:00.480 --> 09:03.440
Yeah, well, Aunt Polly's
close to giving him one.

09:03.520 --> 09:05.480
John and Ada, too, it sounds like.

09:05.560 --> 09:07.880
John moans on bloody principle.

09:07.960 --> 09:09.680
But if you saw his missus...

09:12.840 --> 09:14.640
You have a girl yourself, son?

09:17.960 --> 09:19.840
Perhaps when it suits Tommy, eh?

09:22.000 --> 09:26.920
Yeah, well, he's been different,
you know, since the war.

09:27.000 --> 09:31.040
Yeah, well, a war can change a man.

09:31.120 --> 09:32.880
Speaking for myself, anyway.

09:32.960 --> 09:34.480
Where did you fight, Dad?

09:35.000 --> 09:37.840
Ah, all over, son, all over.

09:37.920 --> 09:39.840
Yeah, all over.

09:39.920 --> 09:44.560
Then the salvation of Jesus Christ
spread His light over me,

09:46.000 --> 09:49.800
and as a pilgrim,
I come to visit the New World.

09:50.320 --> 09:51.760
America.

09:51.840 --> 09:54.200
Where I beheld the future.

09:56.720 --> 10:00.120
Casinos. Money factories, son.

10:00.200 --> 10:03.480
Look, I've been studying the competition,

10:04.960 --> 10:06.440
their schemes,

10:06.520 --> 10:08.840
their systems. Look at that.

10:08.920 --> 10:10.960
-Show me.
-It's all there.

10:11.040 --> 10:13.080
There's a fortune to be made here.

10:15.080 --> 10:18.200
I'm an old man,
and my heart's a battered vessel.

10:18.280 --> 10:19.320
But within...

10:21.280 --> 10:24.240
there still beats
the fluttering pulse of a dream.

10:26.200 --> 10:30.640
The Shelby Casino and Hotel.

10:30.720 --> 10:34.440
Gents and dames
will come flocking from all corners.

10:35.000 --> 10:40.280
New York, Chicago, Boston.
To the Shelby,

10:40.360 --> 10:44.120
where I can stand proudly
with my dear children by my side.

10:45.200 --> 10:46.680
And the women there!

10:48.720 --> 10:52.280
Like fresh peaches.
Thou could have a dozen.

10:55.480 --> 10:57.800
We'd all of us be kings!

10:57.880 --> 10:59.880
How much? How much to get started?

11:00.920 --> 11:03.600
The oak needs but an acorn.

11:05.360 --> 11:06.680
Let's do it.

11:07.600 --> 11:09.720
Let's do it. Let's bloody do it.

11:09.800 --> 11:11.640
It would make my heart beam,

11:11.720 --> 11:14.760
but I don't want to cause
any discord between the brothers.

11:14.840 --> 11:17.720
So, please, why don't you
talk to Tommy first.

11:17.800 --> 11:20.640
No, no, I'm sick of taking
orders from him.

11:20.720 --> 11:23.920
Tommy's not the only one
in the family with a head for business.

11:25.800 --> 11:30.280
And Shelby money is Shelby money.

11:30.360 --> 11:33.840
I thank God for my wonderful sons.

11:35.720 --> 11:37.960
This is cause for a celebration!

11:38.040 --> 11:39.600
-Yeah.
-Sláinte!

11:39.680 --> 11:40.800
Sláinte!

11:47.200 --> 11:48.600
On your feet, soldier.

11:50.480 --> 11:51.640
On your feet!

11:54.880 --> 11:56.680
[all shouting]

11:59.280 --> 12:00.640
I don't want to fight you, Dad.

12:00.720 --> 12:03.520
Come on, boy!
I'm old enough to be your father.

12:13.680 --> 12:15.480
On your feet.

12:15.840 --> 12:16.880
Get up!

12:18.080 --> 12:19.120
All right!

12:30.680 --> 12:32.280
Is that all you've got, boy?

12:39.280 --> 12:40.360
Get up!

12:51.720 --> 12:55.520
This here is Arthur Shelby Jr.!

12:55.600 --> 12:59.720
My son! I love him, and I'm proud of him.

12:59.800 --> 13:02.720
And he can fight any one of youse in here!

13:02.800 --> 13:04.000
[crowd cheering]

13:10.800 --> 13:13.920
You did good, son. You did good.

13:14.000 --> 13:16.720
I love you, Dad! I love you!

13:35.720 --> 13:37.080
Mr. Shelby?

13:38.560 --> 13:39.880
Who's asking?

13:40.680 --> 13:41.760
My name is Byrne.

13:43.560 --> 13:46.720
I had word from your man
in Camden Town you wanted to parley.

13:48.200 --> 13:49.600
Then parley it is.

13:52.000 --> 13:54.760
A few months ago,
a man named Ryan came to this place

13:54.840 --> 13:57.480
with a view to buying
some goods from you.

13:57.560 --> 13:59.800
Mr. Ryan met with an accident.
He was shot.

14:00.280 --> 14:01.840
I heard.

14:01.920 --> 14:04.440
[Byrne] He was a man
with a quick mouth. I know that.

14:05.040 --> 14:07.040
I wondered if he made
any enemies in here.

14:07.120 --> 14:08.960
None that I know of.

14:09.040 --> 14:11.200
It's not the kind of place
to make enemies.

14:11.280 --> 14:12.720
All are welcome here, Mr. Byrne.

14:12.800 --> 14:14.200
Including Irish?

14:14.280 --> 14:15.760
Oh, especially Irish.

14:17.960 --> 14:21.120
Ryan told you he was a member
of the Irish Republican Army.

14:21.200 --> 14:23.240
Was he still welcome?

14:23.320 --> 14:25.800
Like I say, any man
that buys beer is welcome.

14:25.880 --> 14:27.680
Perhaps you didn't believe him.

14:33.080 --> 14:38.000
In pubs, sometimes people say things,
sometimes it's the whiskey talking.

14:38.080 --> 14:39.920
It's hard to tell which is which.

14:41.680 --> 14:44.520
As a teetotal man, I find that amusing.

14:44.600 --> 14:47.200
Except when it ends in tragedy.

14:47.280 --> 14:49.320
Would you like some water
and cordial, Mr. Byrne?

14:49.400 --> 14:54.080
You see, Mr. Shelby,
Ryan, for all his quick mouth,

14:54.160 --> 14:56.800
was indeed connected.

14:56.880 --> 14:59.800
Very well connected to our brotherhood.

14:59.880 --> 15:03.040
By membership and blood.
He was my cousin.

15:04.960 --> 15:06.560
I am from South Armagh.

15:08.560 --> 15:11.400
I'm a man of influence there.

15:11.480 --> 15:13.760
Cordial and water
would be grand, Mr. Shelby.

15:17.200 --> 15:19.800
Grace, bring some water and cordial
to the snug.

15:19.880 --> 15:21.560
-This way.
-Yes, Mr. Shelby.

15:34.280 --> 15:35.920
My cousin came to buy guns.

15:36.000 --> 15:37.520
And I told him I have none.

15:39.400 --> 15:41.920
Your man, Danny Owen,
talks a lot when he's drunk.

15:44.000 --> 15:46.160
He says the Peaky Blinders
do have the guns.

15:46.400 --> 15:48.480
Robbed from the factory down the road.

15:48.560 --> 15:50.480
He boasts about
a stack of Lewis machine guns

15:50.560 --> 15:54.200
and enough belts of ammunition
to hold up God's trousers.

15:54.280 --> 15:59.520
Yep. That sounds like our Danny.
He has an imagination.

15:59.600 --> 16:03.480
Like I say, sometimes it's the whiskey
that does the talking.

16:13.680 --> 16:16.160
He says only the brothers know
where the guns are kept.

16:16.240 --> 16:20.000
Well, Danny also says
he sees German infantrymen

16:20.080 --> 16:22.240
on the back of mill carts.

16:22.320 --> 16:24.280
And he shoots them with his broomstick.

16:26.520 --> 16:29.080
We have men in the BSA factory.

16:30.080 --> 16:32.320
They say it's you who has them.

16:32.400 --> 16:35.440
And we have men
who work in the police station.

16:35.520 --> 16:37.640
Every finger, Mr. Shelby.

16:38.360 --> 16:40.480
Every finger in this city

16:40.560 --> 16:42.280
points in one direction.

16:44.080 --> 16:45.800
Please don't mistake me for a fool.

17:02.080 --> 17:03.800
Let me get to the point.

17:04.160 --> 17:07.480
I don't care what kind
of half-arsed tinker operation

17:07.560 --> 17:11.920
you have going here.
But I can assure you,

17:12.000 --> 17:14.960
I represent a very different category
of organization.

17:17.960 --> 17:19.440
My cousin was shot.

17:21.480 --> 17:24.960
I am judge, jury and executioner.

17:25.040 --> 17:27.400
I find you guilty, and I pass sentence.

17:28.480 --> 17:30.160
You deliver the guns to me,

17:31.280 --> 17:34.760
or I deliver death and hell's fury to you

17:34.840 --> 17:36.600
and your little tribe of heathens.

17:37.480 --> 17:39.240
Am I making myself clear?

17:52.720 --> 17:54.640
Let me confess something to you.

17:55.320 --> 17:56.880
And only to you.

17:58.960 --> 18:00.080
I have the guns,

18:01.480 --> 18:03.200
but they have become a burden to me.

18:06.080 --> 18:09.000
Perhaps it is time to unload that burden.

18:10.680 --> 18:12.240
For the right price.

18:27.280 --> 18:28.920
[clears throat]

18:37.840 --> 18:39.920
[Campbell] Malacki Byrne.

18:40.000 --> 18:43.240
Brigade commander
of the South Armagh IRA.

18:45.000 --> 18:46.480
You hooked yourself a big fish there.

18:46.560 --> 18:49.560
With these guns as bait,
who knows what we'll catch?

18:49.640 --> 18:51.560
"We."

18:51.640 --> 18:55.720
Are you suggesting that you and I
could work together as a team?

18:55.800 --> 18:58.680
Perhaps we have more in common
than you think, Inspector.

18:59.880 --> 19:01.360
Can you deliver him?

19:01.440 --> 19:03.200
With your help.

19:03.280 --> 19:06.440
And I want word put out in Ireland
that I was not involved.

19:08.160 --> 19:11.120
[Campbell] So I'd be solving
a problem for you.

19:11.200 --> 19:14.280
-And I'd be winning you that medal.
-[laughs]

19:14.360 --> 19:15.760
If I get a medal,

19:15.840 --> 19:18.880
I will have your initials
engraved on the backside.

19:21.400 --> 19:25.040
My initials on your backside.
That's quite an image.

19:27.440 --> 19:30.800
Inspector, since we're getting on so well,

19:30.880 --> 19:32.800
can you answer me a question?

19:32.880 --> 19:34.480
Who gave you Freddie Thorne?

19:35.640 --> 19:37.720
As everyone in the city knows,

19:38.840 --> 19:41.400
it was you, Mr. Shelby.

19:56.240 --> 19:57.600
[tapping on door]

20:09.880 --> 20:10.960
Hello, son.

20:12.760 --> 20:13.960
It's all there.

20:16.320 --> 20:18.560
It is indeed.

20:18.640 --> 20:20.960
We're gonna build something
with this, son.

20:21.040 --> 20:22.680
Something magnificent.

20:22.760 --> 20:24.240
When do we sail, Dad?

20:24.320 --> 20:26.240
-Hungry for work, are you?
-Yeah.

20:26.320 --> 20:28.720
A ship sails Friday.
Meet me at the boxing ring.

20:28.800 --> 20:30.760
Good. Friday.

20:30.840 --> 20:32.280
Friday.

20:49.240 --> 20:50.360
[banging on door]

21:05.880 --> 21:07.320
Leave that open.

21:18.800 --> 21:19.880
No.

21:19.960 --> 21:21.960
-Are you expecting trouble?
-Yeah.

21:22.040 --> 21:24.720
-At this hour?
-Midnight is as good an hour as any.

21:24.800 --> 21:25.800
What the hell is going on?

21:25.880 --> 21:28.800
When the St. Andrew's bell
strikes midnight,

21:28.880 --> 21:31.400
two IRA men are gonna come
through that door.

21:31.480 --> 21:34.600
When they have what they want,
they plan to kill me.

21:34.680 --> 21:36.760
It's your job to stop that happening.

21:36.840 --> 21:38.400
You could've given me some more warning.

21:38.480 --> 21:40.480
I just got the message myself.

21:40.560 --> 21:42.920
-They want to meet here alone.
-And barmaids don't count?

21:43.000 --> 21:47.160
No. Barmaids don't count.
Now, you're gonna be in that back room.

21:47.240 --> 21:49.840
I'm gonna be sitting there.
When I make a toast,

21:49.920 --> 21:51.360
you're gonna come out
with that thing raised.

21:51.440 --> 21:54.000
You don't shoot. You just point.
I'll do the rest.

21:55.680 --> 21:57.960
-Will you kill them?
-No, the police want them alive.

21:58.040 --> 22:00.960
-The police know about this?
-Look, just hold it up.

22:01.040 --> 22:03.120
Just point. Right?

22:05.040 --> 22:06.760
All right, go. Go on. Go!

22:22.680 --> 22:23.800
[bell dinging]

22:33.160 --> 22:35.120
We'll hold back here.

22:35.200 --> 22:38.960
If damage is done to either side,
it's no concern of ours.

23:12.560 --> 23:13.800
Lost your thirst, eh?

23:14.600 --> 23:16.320
Just show us where.

23:22.040 --> 23:23.560
Give me the cash.

23:33.720 --> 23:35.680
You're gonna need a shovel.

23:44.880 --> 23:47.560
[chuckles]

23:48.240 --> 23:52.200
You thick fucking tinker.
Did you think we'd let you live?

23:53.880 --> 23:56.080
Make your peace, Mr. Shelby.

23:59.960 --> 24:01.880
I will make my peace my own way.

24:07.800 --> 24:09.440
To barmaids who don't count.

24:18.920 --> 24:20.160
[both grunting]

24:53.200 --> 24:54.520
[breathing heavily]

26:04.560 --> 26:05.920
Why did you shoot?

26:07.040 --> 26:09.360
Why did you shoot, Grace?

26:09.440 --> 26:11.600
I didn't know I had it in me like that.

26:14.480 --> 26:16.000
Now you've seen me.

26:19.960 --> 26:21.240
And you've seen me.

26:24.160 --> 26:25.240
I'm sorry.

26:43.480 --> 26:45.800
You were supposed to come
on the sixth chime.

26:45.880 --> 26:48.600
You were supposed to come
on the fucking sixth chime!

26:55.160 --> 26:56.720
They refused to surrender.

26:59.160 --> 27:01.280
They fought well. They were brave men.

27:03.200 --> 27:06.600
Well, he looks like he was killed
by a wild fucking animal.

27:08.080 --> 27:14.720
Still, this never happened.
They were never here. Who cares?

27:14.800 --> 27:16.720
Get the bodies out of here.

27:16.800 --> 27:19.960
Ah, right, are they making
the lady uncomfortable?

27:21.600 --> 27:23.800
I'll leave you two lovebirds
to it, then, eh?

28:12.640 --> 28:13.640
Thank you.

28:18.040 --> 28:19.120
I'm sorry.

28:57.680 --> 29:00.440
First of all, let me say,

29:00.520 --> 29:03.400
I had no idea he would involve you
in this ugly business.

29:03.480 --> 29:06.560
If I had, I never
would have let it happen.

29:06.640 --> 29:09.880
He trusts me. I told you that.
You didn't believe me.

29:10.480 --> 29:11.800
Fine.

29:13.120 --> 29:16.680
Sergeant Moss made a report,
which, of course, I burnt.

29:16.760 --> 29:20.160
He said, when he entered
the room, you were embracing.

29:21.880 --> 29:24.760
Is that your primary concern?
An embrace?

29:26.520 --> 29:28.840
No, my concern is for your welfare.

29:28.920 --> 29:30.120
It was me who killed them.

29:32.640 --> 29:34.960
I had no control.

29:35.040 --> 29:37.080
You have been living with beasts.

29:38.880 --> 29:40.800
It was the beast that tried to stop me.

29:48.320 --> 29:51.400
I believe last night
something inside me changed.

29:52.160 --> 29:54.760
I no longer feel the need
to avenge my father.

29:55.680 --> 29:58.240
The hatred that I brought here
with me is gone.

30:00.080 --> 30:02.560
And therefore, my reasons
for joining the service.

30:03.000 --> 30:04.440
You want to resign?

30:06.160 --> 30:08.360
I think our mission
has come to a natural end.

30:11.000 --> 30:13.640
I think I know where the guns are hidden.

30:13.720 --> 30:15.720
You do? So tell me where.

30:15.800 --> 30:17.400
If I'm right and the guns are found,

30:17.480 --> 30:20.920
you have no more business
with Thomas Shelby. Is that not so?

30:21.000 --> 30:24.720
Our military mission will be over,
and we can leave the city as we found it.

30:26.280 --> 30:28.040
Are you trying to do a deal with me?

30:28.120 --> 30:32.320
Because if you are, you must be explicit.

30:32.400 --> 30:36.040
I want your word that Thomas Shelby
will not be harmed

30:36.120 --> 30:39.240
if the guns are recovered.
Your word as a gentleman.

30:40.360 --> 30:41.560
Will you give it?

30:41.640 --> 30:43.600
Now, why would you want to save him?

30:45.840 --> 30:47.920
A residue of sympathy.

30:48.000 --> 30:50.040
Sympathy? You mean sentiment?

30:51.360 --> 30:53.080
Yes.

30:53.160 --> 30:56.000
In his way, he has been kind to me.

30:56.080 --> 30:58.800
-Sentiment.
-Yes.

31:05.240 --> 31:07.320
You're too good-hearted for this work.

31:09.080 --> 31:10.480
Perhaps.

31:11.720 --> 31:13.480
So, for my sake, will you spare him?

31:16.160 --> 31:17.560
You have my word.

31:21.480 --> 31:23.440
A week after the robbery,
there was a burial

31:23.520 --> 31:26.080
at St. Andrew's churchyard.

31:26.160 --> 31:30.280
I have found out that the man
supposed to be buried is alive.

31:30.360 --> 31:32.760
Arthur is quite transparent.

31:32.840 --> 31:37.200
I learned that the funeral was
attended only by the brothers.

31:37.280 --> 31:40.600
And the grave that they dug
was far deeper than your average

31:40.680 --> 31:42.880
and lined with lead.

31:42.960 --> 31:44.680
To keep out the damp.

31:47.600 --> 31:49.840
The guns are buried in that grave.

31:51.920 --> 31:54.240
Then tonight we will dig up that grave.

31:57.000 --> 32:00.560
[Grace] ♪ When my family thinks ♪

32:00.640 --> 32:04.360
♪ That I'm safely in my bed ♪

32:04.440 --> 32:08.320
♪ Oh, from morn until night ♪

32:08.400 --> 32:12.440
♪ I am stretched out at your head ♪

32:12.520 --> 32:17.000
♪ Calling out unto the earth ♪

32:17.080 --> 32:20.480
♪ With tears hot and wild ♪

32:20.560 --> 32:25.040
♪ For the loss of a boy ♪

32:26.280 --> 32:29.960
♪ That I loved as a child ♪

32:32.360 --> 32:36.400
♪ So I am stretched on your grave ♪

32:36.480 --> 32:40.160
♪ And I'll lie here forever ♪

32:40.240 --> 32:43.400
♪ If your hands were in mine ♪

32:43.480 --> 32:48.440
♪ I'd be sure they would not sever ♪

32:48.520 --> 32:52.680
♪ My apple tree, my brightness ♪

32:53.680 --> 32:56.560
♪ It's time we were together ♪

32:56.640 --> 32:57.880
Well done, boys.

32:57.960 --> 33:01.360
♪ For I smell of the earth ♪

33:03.160 --> 33:07.280
♪ And I'm worn by the weather ♪

33:16.640 --> 33:18.360
All but one gun accounted for.

33:29.120 --> 33:31.440
Then, sir, I resign my commission.

33:34.040 --> 33:35.400
Good.

33:36.280 --> 33:37.640
Good.

33:39.440 --> 33:44.240
So I am no longer your superior officer,

33:44.320 --> 33:46.920
and you are no longer my subordinate.

33:48.400 --> 33:49.560
And therefore,

33:52.200 --> 33:56.680
regulations permit me to offer you this.

34:04.400 --> 34:08.360
I'm a... I'm a simple man but a good man.

34:09.840 --> 34:13.080
And my admiration for you

34:13.159 --> 34:14.480
has turned to love.

34:16.719 --> 34:20.480
I don't ask for love in return. Just...

34:20.560 --> 34:23.320
recognition that we are like minds

34:24.760 --> 34:26.239
with shared values.

34:27.960 --> 34:29.000
Grace,

34:30.760 --> 34:32.080
will you marry me?

34:45.199 --> 34:46.360
Mr. Campbell...

34:51.080 --> 34:52.480
you deserve better.

35:04.120 --> 35:05.280
Is it him between us?

35:06.680 --> 35:09.360
Is it the beast that dug that grave?

35:09.440 --> 35:11.240
Is it him?!

35:12.680 --> 35:15.000
My resignation will be with you
in the morning.

35:34.960 --> 35:36.240
Dad?

35:40.160 --> 35:41.560
Hello, son.

35:42.360 --> 35:44.120
May I ask who gave you
my whereabouts?

35:44.200 --> 35:46.080
Marston.

35:46.160 --> 35:48.720
Said you left him last night
with a bill for your whores.

35:48.800 --> 35:51.120
Well, at least we got to say goodbye, son.

35:52.680 --> 35:55.600
And bid a fond adieu
to your dear brothers, would you?

35:57.000 --> 35:58.640
How could you do this to us?

35:58.720 --> 35:59.760
Do what, son?

35:59.840 --> 36:04.320
All that stuff you said
about the Shelby Casino.

36:05.960 --> 36:08.280
And Atlantic City.

36:08.360 --> 36:11.520
Well, if the truth be told,
I'm not so acquainted

36:11.600 --> 36:14.080
with that promised land
as I had thee believe.

36:17.800 --> 36:21.920
You're a fucking liar and a thief.

36:22.000 --> 36:24.320
You give me back my fucking money!

36:25.360 --> 36:28.080
"Do not despise the thief

36:28.160 --> 36:30.840
who steals to satisfy his starvation."

36:32.360 --> 36:34.120
That's in the Holy Bible, son.

36:35.360 --> 36:38.320
And I have starved for so very long.

36:40.840 --> 36:42.920
Fare thee well, son.

36:46.920 --> 36:48.400
I waited for you.

36:50.680 --> 36:52.280
I waited.

36:53.280 --> 36:55.600
[shouting]

36:55.680 --> 36:58.120
Listen to me, boy.

36:58.200 --> 37:00.440
You are not in the prize ring now.

37:00.520 --> 37:04.160
If you ever put your hands on me again,
I'll cut your fucking throat

37:04.240 --> 37:06.680
and spread you on these tracks.

37:47.040 --> 37:48.360
Where's your father?

37:54.000 --> 37:56.760
I'm assuming he's frittering away
the 500 you took from us

37:56.840 --> 37:59.880
and put in his thieving,
whore-groping hands.

38:02.600 --> 38:04.080
What were you thinking?

38:05.440 --> 38:08.880
How dare you do something like that
without talking to Thomas or me?

38:12.520 --> 38:13.920
Does Tommy know?

38:23.000 --> 38:24.680
No.

38:24.760 --> 38:26.120
But you're gonna tell him.

38:27.560 --> 38:29.800
You might take satisfaction

38:30.680 --> 38:32.800
in a great victory.

38:32.880 --> 38:35.600
A terrible consequence has been avoided.

38:37.240 --> 38:41.520
Those guns that we dug up will never
be used to murder the innocent

38:42.560 --> 38:45.080
or usurp the status quo.

38:45.160 --> 38:47.280
But even though we have solved a crime,

38:47.360 --> 38:51.640
we have as yet failed
to punish the criminal.

38:51.720 --> 38:57.040
This man who dug this grave
has also dug his own.

38:57.120 --> 39:01.840
He has proved a deadly menace
to the King's peace.

39:01.920 --> 39:03.960
And tonight we will strike him down.

39:04.040 --> 39:07.840
We will drive our sword
through his black heart.

39:07.920 --> 39:12.280
We will pursue him
into the ratholes that he infests.

39:12.360 --> 39:17.640
And finally, we will rid
this city of his kind.

39:17.720 --> 39:21.720
Justice will be done
and will be seen to be done.

39:24.000 --> 39:25.120
Amen.

39:27.960 --> 39:30.160
There's gonna be trouble now, Finn.

39:30.240 --> 39:32.360
You look after yourself, do you hear me?

39:32.440 --> 39:35.000
I'm gonna be going away for a while.

39:35.080 --> 39:36.440
Right. Go on.

39:44.280 --> 39:48.440
Right! Who wants to fucking fight?

39:48.520 --> 39:52.080
Fighting's over.
We're closing up and moving on.

39:52.160 --> 39:54.680
I said, who wants to fucking fight?

39:54.760 --> 39:58.880
My name is Arthur fucking Shelby!

40:03.800 --> 40:05.880
Who dare fight me?

40:05.960 --> 40:08.680
Go home, lad,
before you catch yourself a spanking.

40:20.720 --> 40:23.040
My brother in Digbeth just said
the police are coming down

40:23.120 --> 40:26.880
from Deritend in numbers,
asking for Tommy Shelby by name.

40:29.440 --> 40:31.000
Shit.

40:40.520 --> 40:42.080
I'm gonna have to lie low for a while.

40:42.160 --> 40:44.160
-Why?
-I lost my bargaining power.

40:44.240 --> 40:47.160
This copper, it's just me and him now.

40:47.240 --> 40:48.560
When I get back,

40:50.000 --> 40:51.320
I'm gonna tell you some things.

40:51.400 --> 40:53.400
Harry said the police
are already in Digbeth.

40:53.480 --> 40:54.640
Yeah.

40:54.720 --> 40:57.400
You took a chance coming here. Why?

40:57.480 --> 40:59.240
The police are in the lane, Tommy!

41:00.400 --> 41:02.000
Come with me.

42:15.680 --> 42:18.440
I'm looking for Thomas Shelby.

42:26.800 --> 42:27.920
Never heard of him.

42:33.800 --> 42:35.200
You'll never find him.

42:43.600 --> 42:44.880
Go home.

42:52.400 --> 42:54.680
Perhaps I should ask that question again.

42:55.960 --> 42:57.040
On your knees.

42:57.120 --> 42:58.920
[grunting]

43:03.720 --> 43:07.320
Now, understand this, barman.

43:07.400 --> 43:09.320
I don't care if you live or die.

43:10.000 --> 43:11.640
I don't know!

43:22.000 --> 43:23.480
He left.

43:24.320 --> 43:25.400
With the barmaid.

43:27.320 --> 43:28.880
He left with Grace.

43:30.680 --> 43:32.440
I think they were going to her place.

43:40.840 --> 43:42.840
Call it off.

43:42.920 --> 43:45.200
I don't understand, sir.
We should find the barmaid and--

43:45.280 --> 43:46.440
Call it off!

43:48.040 --> 43:49.080
All of it!

43:51.720 --> 43:53.000
Get in!

44:09.040 --> 44:10.720
It's not much of a place.

44:11.920 --> 44:13.400
It's all right.

44:13.480 --> 44:14.480
You want tea?

44:14.560 --> 44:16.440
Tea? No.

44:16.520 --> 44:18.160
I have rum.

44:18.240 --> 44:20.000
Actually, tea it is.

44:20.080 --> 44:21.200
You want to impress me?

44:21.280 --> 44:24.080
Yes. And do you have a biscuit?

44:24.560 --> 44:25.960
No. They attract mice.

44:28.200 --> 44:30.040
People look different at home.

44:30.120 --> 44:31.560
In what way?

44:31.640 --> 44:32.920
Off guard.

44:36.840 --> 44:38.440
Should I be on my guard?

44:38.520 --> 44:40.960
No, I'm a man who drinks tea.

44:55.000 --> 44:56.960
When the trouble dies down, I'll go.

45:04.600 --> 45:07.280
When will it die down, do you think?

45:07.360 --> 45:09.200
Late, I'd say.

45:12.520 --> 45:14.680
So not until the morning, then.

45:16.760 --> 45:18.800
Yes. I'd say I'll be here till morning.

45:26.400 --> 45:28.520
-You have a gramophone.
-It's broken.

45:28.600 --> 45:30.080
We could still dance.

45:35.000 --> 45:36.000
Yes. Why not?

45:42.320 --> 45:44.360
I know you like to be asked properly.

45:47.000 --> 45:48.840
Grace, can I have this dance?

48:01.480 --> 48:03.680
[Grace] Are you okay?

48:03.760 --> 48:05.960
[Thomas] I don't hear
the shovels against the wall.

48:08.400 --> 48:09.600
[Grace] What shovels?

48:13.800 --> 48:15.080
Will you help me?

48:17.280 --> 48:18.600
[Grace] Help you with what?

48:18.680 --> 48:19.920
With everything.

48:21.360 --> 48:23.680
The whole fucking thing.

48:23.760 --> 48:26.760
Fucking life, business.

48:29.680 --> 48:31.040
I found you.

48:33.080 --> 48:34.360
And you found me.

48:37.560 --> 48:38.960
We'll help each other.

49:29.800 --> 49:31.400
[crying]

49:53.960 --> 49:57.400
Our Father, who art in Heaven.

49:59.120 --> 50:00.760
Hallowed be Thy name.

50:01.880 --> 50:03.680
Thy...

50:06.880 --> 50:07.960
[muffled coughing]

50:32.280 --> 50:35.600
[gasping]

50:40.600 --> 50:41.960
[coughing]

50:50.840 --> 50:52.080
[telephone ringing]

50:55.200 --> 50:58.520
Hello. [clears throat]

50:58.600 --> 51:00.880
Send a telegram to Mr. Churchill.

51:02.200 --> 51:04.160
I have news, very good news.

51:06.200 --> 51:09.600
Tell him the business
I came to attend to is now complete.

51:10.920 --> 51:13.400
I'll be leaving the city.

51:13.480 --> 51:17.600
There's just one matter
I need to tidy up first.

51:34.720 --> 51:35.760
[door opens]

51:57.960 --> 51:59.600
So Polly told you.

52:01.280 --> 52:02.280
Yep.

52:15.520 --> 52:17.120
You should have used a gun.

52:19.800 --> 52:21.320
Are you laughing at me, Tommy?

52:22.120 --> 52:23.160
Yeah.

52:25.280 --> 52:27.920
Just when things
are starting to go right, Arthur,

52:28.800 --> 52:30.240
you try and do this.

52:33.200 --> 52:35.600
Don't you like fancy parties?

52:35.680 --> 52:37.480
Or, um...

52:37.560 --> 52:39.720
Champagne? Or fast cars?

52:42.200 --> 52:43.520
And how about this?

52:48.760 --> 52:51.040
Your name on a business card.

52:51.120 --> 52:55.320
"Shelby Brothers, Limited?

52:55.400 --> 52:59.880
Arthur Shelby. Associate bookmaker."

52:59.960 --> 53:02.880
[Thomas] I just had them picked up
from the printers this morning.

53:02.960 --> 53:05.280
You're one of three shareholders.

53:06.600 --> 53:08.240
Me, you, John.

53:08.320 --> 53:11.440
And according to the law,
we are equal partners.

53:11.520 --> 53:14.720
And it is written in the paperwork
in black and white.

53:14.800 --> 53:17.560
A third, a third, a third.

53:21.200 --> 53:22.560
But the thing is...

53:22.640 --> 53:26.000
Well, me and John,
we quite fancy splitting your share so...

53:26.080 --> 53:28.720
just next time, use a gun, man.

53:33.800 --> 53:36.640
Our men at the station tell me
that copper is leaving town.

53:38.080 --> 53:39.160
We're in the clear.

53:42.680 --> 53:44.640
We're on our way up in the world, brother.

53:47.680 --> 53:48.760
Believe me.
